5. Application Specifications

a. Architecture
The system follows a three-tier architecture consisting of a frontend (user interface), backend (business logic), and database.
The frontend is a mobile application where students and landlords can register, search for apartments, view listings, and communicate through chat.
The backend handles the main functionality of the system, including user authentication, managing listings, processing search requests, and handling messages between users.
The database stores all the data such as user information, apartment listings, messages, and saved favorites.
The frontend sends requests to the backend (for example, when a user searches for an apartment or sends a message). The backend processes the request, communicates with the database to retrieve or store data, and then sends the response back to the frontend, where it is displayed to the user.

b. Database Model
The database includes tables such as Users, Listings, Messages, Favorites, and Reports.
Each user can be either a student, landlord, or admin, and all users are stored in the Users table. Each listing is created by a landlord and is linked to the Users table using a foreign key.
Students can save multiple listings as favorites, and this relationship is stored in the Favorites table. Users can also send messages to each other, and these are stored in the Messages table, where each message is linked to both a sender and a receiver.
Reports are created by users when they report a listing or another user, and each report is linked to the user who created it.
The email field in the Users table is unique, ensuring no duplicate accounts. All listings must reference a valid landlord, and all messages and favorites must reference valid users. This ensures data integrity and consistency across the system.

c. Technologies Used
The system is developed using Python for backend development due to its simplicity and ability to handle server-side logic. The frontend is built using React Native, which allows the application to run on both Android and iOS devices from a single codebase. MySQL is used as the database for efficient and structured data management. These technologies were selected because they are widely used, easy to implement, and suitable for building scalable and responsive mobile applications.

d. User Interface Design
The interface is designed as a mobile application for students and landlords. Students can browse apartment listings, search and filter results, save favorite listings, and communicate with other users through an in-app messaging feature. Landlords can create and manage apartment listings.
The interface includes a login and registration page, a home page with apartment listings, a search and filter page, a listing details page, and a user profile page. Messaging and communication are integrated within the application when users interact with each other.
The design is simple and user-friendly, with clear navigation and buttons for key actions such as searching, saving listings, and contacting landlords. The layout is optimized for mobile devices to ensure ease of use for students.

e. Security Measures
The system uses user authentication to ensure that only registered users can access the platform. Each user must log in with a valid email and password. Passwords are securely stored using encryption (hashing) to protect user data from unauthorized access. Role-based access control is implemented so that students, landlords, and administrators have different permissions within the system. For example, only landlords can create and manage listings, while only admins can manage users and reports. All data sent between the frontend and backend is secured using HTTPS to protect communication between the client and server from interception or tampering. Additionally, user sessions expire automatically after a period of inactivity to prevent unauthorized access to accounts.
